{"id":"548274414","kind":"article","title":"变得无聊","author":"Andy Matuschak","original_authors":["Andy Matuschak"],"original_source_urls":["https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zrQz6Eqcnrf3QqEf4A92J5bMSwED9KtMZje"],"publisher":"Jarrett Ye","column":"常青笔记 & 知识工作","date":"2022-07-31","updated":"2023-07-08","votes":27,"comment_count":2,"minutes":1,"chars":323,"keywords":["无聊","好奇心","创造力","闲暇"],"summary":"短文建议，无聊时先别立刻用阅读、任务或网络填满空闲；作者认为，容忍一段空白有时是重新变得好奇的前提。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/548274414","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"链接至本文（已汉化）"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"声明"}],"html":"<p data-pid=\"TMTWNlaZ\">用活动填补空闲时间诱人至极：阅读书籍，执行任务，网络冲浪，即时聊天。<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zDoZS3Wt316napbdaBGU8C8WLVuyPeAu5Bi\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">用别人的想法填满闲暇时间是一种文化习惯</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>；为了给自己腾出空间，我必须适应“空虚”的时间。我发现我经常在能<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zKvtqpdyujNByokN4fSahKrgNgXxCAWD5gRv\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">变得好奇</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>之前不得不先变得无聊。</p><p data-pid=\"CfIaIf25\">所以我的忠告是：当你觉得无聊时，保持这种感觉，而不是立即伸手去看书或做其他活动。</p><p data-pid=\"cY-mc8NS\">相关笔记：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z8BENejnm5iyqRUodaqyScehdgnuu9b1vn669\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">拘泥于「专注」会损害创造性工作</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup></p><h2 id=\"sec-1\">链接至本文（已汉化）</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"YPSzdkLG\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"622642769\" href=\"#/post/622642769\">用别人的想法填满闲暇时间是一种文化习惯</a></li><li data-pid=\"jWRYoQ6E\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"642001316\" href=\"#/post/642001316\">倾听自己的想法很难</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-2\">声明</h2><p data-pid=\"a1kSLiu9\">此内容发布由 Andy Matuschak 许可。未经允许，不得转载或修改。保留所有权利。</p><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"6TvUp4Ep\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"http://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zrQz6Eqcnrf3QqEf4A92J5bMSwED9KtMZje\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Get bored (andymatuschak.org)</a></blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 用别人的想法填满闲暇时间是一种文化习惯 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"622642769\" href=\"#/post/622642769\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 变得好奇 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"575633658\" href=\"#/post/575633658\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 太过执迷「专注」反而不利于创造性工作 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"628439036\" href=\"#/post/628439036\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"546882133","title":"专注的软件开发工作是自我否定的","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":16,"minutes":2,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 常青笔记 & 知识工作"},{"id":"548549119","title":"变得好玩","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":12,"minutes":1,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 常青笔记 & 知识工作"},{"id":"642001316","title":"倾听自己的想法很难","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":31,"minutes":3,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"575633658","title":"变得好奇","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":22,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"628439036","title":"太过执迷「专注」反而不利于创造性工作","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":25,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[{"id":"676452556","title":"《辞去你的工作》Wolf Tivy","author":"Wolf Tivy","votes":39,"minutes":6,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「好奇心」· Wolf Tivy"}],"rec_answers":[]}